@startuml
!include ../_style.iuml
title Epic 4 — The phone app (camera + display)

rectangle "Phone app (realme, ARCore)" {
  card US4_1 [
    **US-4.1  Record a session for development**
    As a //developer//, I want to record video, pose, depth and camera intrinsics to files,
    so that I can replay the same scene while I build and test.
    ----
    * One folder per session; replay.py reads it like any dataset (same Frame type as TUM).
    * Timestamps of RGB, pose and depth line up per frame.
  ]
  card US4_2 [
    **US-4.2  Stream live to the laptop**
    As a //user//, I want the phone to send what it sees to the laptop server,
    so that the heavy models run on the GPU, not on the phone.
    ----
    * JPEG frames + ARCore 6-DoF pose (+ Depth API map + intrinsics) over a WebSocket.
    * Works over Wi-Fi or USB tethering; reconnects on its own.
  ]
  card US4_3 [
    **US-4.3  Ask and see the answer on the phone**
    As a //user//, I want to type or say my question on the phone and see the reply there,
    so that the phone is the only thing I hold.
    ----
    * The screen shows the answer text, the last-seen keyframe, live directions and the mask overlay.
    * Query to first answer in under 2 seconds.
  ]
}
US4_1 -[hidden]down- US4_2
US4_2 -[hidden]down- US4_3
@enduml
